argaryen's  kingsguard but later on he does become  the lord commander of the kingsguard  now if you really want to learn what  these new characters will do in house of  the dragon i would highly recommend  watching one of my more recent videos  where i explain the main story of this  series  i basically go over all the major events  that will be seen  i will link that video down below the  next character masaria  is a very interesting one if i do say so  myself  she is sort of like the female version  of a varys or littlefinger  so i'm very excited to see what they do  with her she will also be a series  regular  lady misery is a striver and a schemer  she seeks to rise up in a society that  sees her as an outcast  and an outsider her beginnings are as a  sex worker  but she never lets an opportunity slide  and her intelligence and unflagging  ambition will carry her even nearer to  her goal  she wants to have power over the power  full now  it remains to be seen whether she will  use it to gain acceptance or revenge  life in westeros is a game and she wants  to win it  that sounds exactly like a character we  already know in fact  you will notice that a lot most of these  characters are very similar to some of  the characters we have already seen  in game of thrones she is also known for  having a relationship with king viserys  targaryen's brother daemon  so we will most likely see a lot of her  in house of the dragon  the next character on this list is  rhaenys targaryen  who will also be a series regular it  says she is wise and cultured  the queen who never was she was passed  over for the iron throne simply because  she wasn't a man  she is clever capable spirited and proud  she is the embodiment of grit and grace  and  is utterly fearless she is also a dragon  rider  she is split between her loyalty to her  husband  and her own feminist aspirations and  disappointments  she struggles with supporting the claim  of the princess  a younger but wilder version of her own  self  who stands to inherit the seven kingdoms  she is a feminist  but also a realist she harbors doubt  that the princess will make a capable  ruler  this character rhaenys has one of the  most epic dragon battles during the  dance of dragons  while on her dragon she fights king  aegon  and his brother aemond while they're on  their own dragons  rhaenys does die during this dragon  fight but not before  severely injuring the king aegon who  never fully recovers from this attack  dragon fought dragons and a second sun  blossomed in the sky when the smoke  cleared  only eamond and vegar stood uninjured  sunfire the most  magnificent dragon in the world had one  of its wings almost completely torn from  its body  trapped beneath sunfire was the king  himself broken and burned so badly in  places that his armor had fused onto his  flesh  again if you want to learn more about  this then i would recommend watching my  other video down below  now the last character on this list is  harold westerling  it says he will be a series regular but  i doubt he will be on the show  as much of the other characters  mentioned he was the lore commander of  the kingsguard  under viserys targaryen in fact it says  he was one of the longest serving  members of the kingsguard  who also had a very successful military  background  there isn't a whole lot of information  on this character  i think the series will focus more on  sir kristin cole  who becomes the lord commander of the  kingsguard after harold westerling  i think that makes more sense because  sir christian cole is there during the  dance of dragons  and he's heavily involved in a lot of  the battles  as i said before this information has  not been confirmed by hbo but i would  almost guarantee we will get an official  announcement soon  these characters influence a lot of the  events during the dance of dragons so we  will have to see them in the new show  in my opinion you cannot do house of the  dragon without them